    "zones": [
      {
        "id": 0,
        "name": "Front Lawn Valve 2",
        "size": 69.72,
        "throughput": 13.4,
        "state": "automatic",
        "bucket": 0,
        "delta": -2.4523969642589947,
        "duration": 0,
        "module": "0",
        "multiplier": 1.0,
        "explanation": "Note: this explanation uses '.' as decimal separator, shows rounded and metric values. Module returned Evapotranspiration deficiency ( = et0 * hour_multiplier + precipitation) of -2.45.Bucket was -7.15.<br/>Maximum bucket size is 24.0.<br/>Drainage rate when saturated (bucket at max) is 50.8.<br/>Current drainage is 0 because [old_bucket] + [delta] <= 0 (-7.15-2.45 = -9.60).<br/>New bucket value is max(0, min([old_bucket] + [delta], max_bucket) - [drainage]) = max(0, min(-7.15-2.45, 24.0) - 0.00) = -9.60.<br/>Since bucket < 0, irrigation is necessary.<br/>To calculate the exact duration, the following steps were taken:<br/><ol><li>The precipitation rate is defined as [throughput] * 60 / [size] = 13.4 * 60 / 69.7 = 11.5.</li><li>The duration is calculated as abs([bucket]) / [precipitation_rate] * 3600 = 9.60 / 11.5 * 3600 = 2996.</li><li>Now, the multiplier is applied. The multiplier is 1.0, hence the duration is 2996.</li><li>Then, the maximum duration is applied. The maximum duration is 5400.</li><li>Finally, the lead time is applied. The lead time is 0.0, hence the final duration is 2996</li></ol>hence the final duration is 2996.</li></ol>",
        "mapping": "0",
        "lead_time": 0.0,
        "maximum_duration": 5400.0,
        "maximum_bucket": 24,
        "last_calculated": "2026-07-27T04:00:01.874593",
        "last_updated": "2026-07-27T10:08:48.878602",
        "number_of_data_points": 4,
        "drainage_rate": 50.8,
        "current_drainage": 0
      }
